mxplorer (@VERSION@) unstable; urgency=low

  * Second alpha.
  * Close the documented functional gaps: copies write a temporary file and
    rename it into place, -p keeps permissions, timestamps, extended
    attributes (ACLs) and hard links, sparse files stay sparse, and the
    interactive path resolves ~user.
  * Search can match file contents (-c), filter by size (-s) and age (-m),
    take several roots at once and stream its results instead of collecting
    them in memory.
  * Fix the edge cases found by the test campaign: -d overflow, unsigned byte
    natural ordering, copying a directory into itself through a symlink, and
    trailing separators in resolved paths.
  * Add core unit tests and end-to-end regression coverage; ctest now runs
    core_operations, core_utils and cli_smoke.

